name w2-07-blindspot
timeout 700
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 7 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE EARLY-WARNING GAP: IS "A RADAR BLIND SPOT" EXPRESSIBLE IN THIS TREE AT ALL?
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none. It stands alone; its cast is disjoint from every other W2 sortie, ground included.
#
# THE ANCHOR: the package "exploited a radar blind spot on the Saudi border", and the Iraqi
# air-defence crews were reported absent at a meal break; no SAM engagement is documented and the only
# fire the raid met was anti-aircraft artillery [T4].
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION, AND THE SPEC ALREADY NAMED THE ALTERNATIVE IT WOULD SETTLE FOR: "without
# terrain masking (`C4`), is 'a radar blind spot' expressible at all - or does the campaign have to
# declare the CAP's `brief_gci` wrong instead of the radar blind?" THE ANSWER IS THE THIRD ONE, AND IT
# IS STRUCTURAL: THERE IS NO CHANNEL FROM AN EARLY-WARNING RADAR TO A FIGHTER TO BE BLIND IN.
#   `C22` (closed 2026-07-28) gives a node a real cue, and it goes over the GROUND command bus to a
#   ground fire unit's antenna. `C6`'s AIRBORNE half is explicitly untouched: a MiG-29 cannot
#   subscribe to anything, and `set brief_gci` is static text an author wrote before the run.
#   So this sortie can measure exactly two things - what the node itself SEES, and what its cue is
#   worth to the one receiver that exists (the site's own AAA) - and it CANNOT measure the anchor's
#   claim, because the anchor's claim is about what the interceptors were told.
# `C4` IS ALSO STILL OPEN AND NOTHING HERE MASKS ANYTHING: the ingress is flown over a flat,
# transparent world, so every detection range below is an UPPER BOUND on what the real border
# geometry would have given, and "a blind spot" has no representation as line of sight either.
#
# WHAT IS DECLARED INSTEAD, and it is the node's own published geometry rather than an invention: an
# early-warning `p18` sits ON the inbound track 200 km short of the dome and radiates (`emcon free`);
# a `zsu23` at the site is its netted member with `autonomy hold`, so the gun engages on the node's
# cue and not otherwise - which makes the cable, and only the cable, decide whether the site's own
# defence ever points the right way. The AAA is the anchor's own and only documented defence.
#
# WHY THE AIR FIGHT IS 2 v 2 AND NOT THE SPEC'S 4 v 2. W1's saturation gate, 2026-07-30: an
# air-to-air result above two aircraft a side is a FIXED POINT in this tree, and the spec's four-ship
# would have produced an outcome no lever on either side could have changed. Cut to 2 v 2, which is
# the boundary. THE AIR HALF IS STILL EXPECTED TO SATURATE and the campaign says so; the quantity
# this file is read for is the NET's traffic, which does not.
#
# THE ARENA: the raid's inbound track, bearing 068.37 deg, from 300 km short of the dome inward.
#   `w2nod7` p18          32.53774 42.53157 - the early-warning node, 200 km short of the dome
#   `w2ewv7` target_soft  32.53774 42.53157 - the node's own van, the aim point of BOTH strikers
#   `w2dom7` target_hard  32.53708 42.52959 - a hardened shelter 200 m from it, the second aim point
#   `w2flk7` zsu23        33.19172 44.49505 - the site's AAA at Al-Tuwaitha, netted, on hold
#   `w2mg71` mig29        33.53113 45.51985 - CAP, 100 km BEYOND the dome
#   `w2mg72` mig29        33.52000 45.54000 - its wingman
# THE CAP IS BEYOND THE TARGET AND NOT BETWEEN, AND THAT IS O1'S RULE APPLIED RATHER THAN OBEYED BY
# LUCK: MEASURED, a CAP 150 km short of the dome killed the lead striker at t = 268.4 s, 165 s before
# its own release, and `FirstFlightKo` ended the run there. The strikers now release at ~433 s and the
# nearest merge is 400 km of closure away.
#
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm): `C5` half closed - the
# tank exists, AERIAL REFUELLING DOES NOT; `C20` open, `--elev const`, a 0 m plane under a route whose
# real ground is 42.83-1,599.22 m (MEASURED); `C10` level laydown; `C7` no F-15 - not needed, both
# sides fly their own types; `FirstFlightKo` - the lead striker's aim point is 100 km short of the
# CAP's own position, so its release comes first by construction; W1's fixed point - declared above.
# Fuel discipline: `set fuel_int_pct`, never `set fuel_pct`.
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 3 is expected. Read, in this order: (1) `net JOIN` / `net CUE` counts
# and the tick of the first one, (2) `site RADIATE` / `site CUE` / `site TRACK` on the node and on the
# gun, and how many bursts the gun fired, (3) the two strikers' `stores DELIVERY` and the ground
# `UNIT_RESULT` lines, (4) the interceptors' first `radar CONTACT` tick against the node's own first
# detection - THE GAP BETWEEN THOSE TWO NUMBERS IS THE MISSING CHANNEL, and it is the sortie's answer.
# Do NOT read the air outcome as a lever's effect: it is a fixed point by W1's measurement.

net tuwaitha
  control w2nod7
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member w2nod7
  member w2flk7 autonomy hold

# MEASURED (fingerprint 7ec2fe1cf5759c1f, exit 0): A BLIND SPOT IS NOT EXPRESSIBLE, AND NOT BECAUSE
# OF `C4`. THERE IS NO CHANNEL BETWEEN THE RADAR AND THE FIGHTERS TO BE BLIND IN.
#   the node      `net JOIN unit=w2flk7 node=w2nod7 distM=196868` at t=3.9, then 12 `net CUE`, the
#                 first at t=8.0 carrying `rngM=294623 altM=240.365 elDeg=0.0467 wcs=free`. THE NODE
#                 HOLDS THE RAID FROM 294.6 km and keeps holding it down to 204.9 km, where the
#                 strikers kill it
#   the receiver  the only one that exists is a ZSU-23-4 at Al-Tuwaitha whose own effective range is
#                 2.5 km. It is told, twelve times, about something 200-295 km away
#   the fighters  `w2mg71`/`w2mg72`, fully briefed (3 `gci BRAA` -> `ENTER_ELEV` -> `ENTER_ZONE` ->
#                 `RADAR_ILLUM` each): `fcr_contacts` MAX 0.0 OVER THE WHOLE 700 s. The gap between
#                 the node's 294.6 km and the fighters' nothing is `C6`'s airborne half, not terrain
#                 masking - a MiG-29 cannot subscribe to anything and `set brief_gci` is text an
#                 author wrote before the run
#   the strike    `w2str9` 11.2135 m on the hardened shelter -> `damage ... rangeM=5.49862
#                 fluxJm2=927396` -> DESTROYED; `w2str8` 27.1881 m -> the van and the node both
#                 DESTROYED. Both strikers SUCCESS, exit 0
#   fuel          both strikers 6,971.8 -> 5,965.7 lb over 100 km of run-in plus egress

unit w2nod7
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 32.53774 42.53157 ground 68.4 0
  set emcon free

unit w2flk7
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 33.19172 44.49505 ground 248.4 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 40

unit w2str8
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight str7 1
  spawn 32.20668 41.54287 240 68.4 450        # 300 km short of the dome
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 32.53774 42.53157 240 450                # THE AIM POINT: the early-warning van itself
  wp 32.30000 41.80000 240 450                # egress back down the track
  objective kill unit w2ewv7
  objective survive

unit w2str9
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight str7 2
  spawn 32.19416 41.54880 240 68.4 450        # 1.5 km across track from the lead
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 32.53708 42.52959 240 450                # THE AIM POINT: the hardened shelter beside the van
  wp 32.30000 41.80000 240 450
  objective kill unit w2dom7
  objective survive

unit w2mg71
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight cap7 1
  spawn 33.53113 45.51985 4000 248.4 450      # CAP on the track, 100 km BEYOND the dome
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission off                       # the documented power-up state: the brief turns it on
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_gci 20 248.4 150 4                # a controller's call, typed by the author before the run
  set brief_gci 60 248.4 100 4                # - and there is no node in this file that could send it
  set brief_gci 100 248.4 60 4
  set task intercept
  wp 32.20668 41.54287 4000 450
  objective survive

unit w2mg72
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight cap7 2
  spawn 33.52000 45.54000 4000 248.4 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_gci 20 248.4 150 4
  set brief_gci 60 248.4 100 4
  set brief_gci 100 248.4 60 4
  set task intercept
  wp 32.20668 41.54287 4000 450
  objective survive

unit w2ewv7
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 32.53774 42.53157 ground 68.4 0

unit w2dom7
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 32.53708 42.52959 ground 68.4 0
